_at":"2025-05-26T16:33:21Z","closed_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106761","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106761.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106761.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:23Z"},"body":"Now that `LocalVector` uses move semantics internally (#100477, #104693) it can also be used to hold move-only types.\r\n\r\n`JoltShapeInstance3D` (through its `ShapeReference` RAII helper) is a good candidate for utilizing this, as it has no reason to ever be copied, and the copies that are currently happening as part of (for example) resizing `JoltObject3D::shapes`[^1] are quite wasteful, as each copy is forced to register and unregister the `JoltObject3D` with the `JoltShape3D`.\r\n\r\nSo this PR simply swaps out its current copy constructor/assignment with a move constructor/assignment instead.\r\n\r\n(There's no real reason to actually `delete` the copy constructor/assignment, but again, there's also no reason for this class to ever be copied, so I'd prefer to just delete them entirely.)\r\n\r\n[^1]: Which I'm realizing now should really live in `JoltShapedObject3D`. I have no idea how that got left behind.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"ht